  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "$$\nf(x)\u223c\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=12{x}^{2}-\\pi $ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ The Fourier cosine series of the **even** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the expression for ${a}_{0}.$\n\n${a}_{0}=$ {{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "For our Fourier cosine series, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=12{x}^{2}-\\pi $ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(12{x}^{2}-\\pi )\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{[12\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-\\pi x]}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }(4{\\pi }^{3}-{\\pi }^{2})-0 \\\\  & =2\\pi (4\\pi -1).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
